  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14689552",
      "title": "Using Inline Functions",
      "lectureOrder": 37,
      "videoOrder": 32,
      "sourceHash": "39512c9c107f3fc20d48ca6f0716e44e3ab20e08458b5ebeb1cb746dd9cbebb4",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 7.87,
          "en": "Talking about event listeners, there's one other quick thing I want to mention.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 7.89,
          "end": 15.63,
          "en": "Thus far, for all the events, I always point it at a function without parentheses to not execute this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 15.63,
          "end": 23.04,
          "en": "when the code gets passed, but to provide a pointer at this function so that when the event occurs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 23.04,
          "end": 24.89,
          "en": "this function can be executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 24.9,
          "end": 30.78,
          "en": "And this would be my recommended way of doing it because this is a really clear way of defining your",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 30.78,
          "end": 32.49,
          "en": "functions up there in the script.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 32.49,
          "end": 36.3,
          "en": "Tags makes it easy for other developers to understand your code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 36.3,
          "end": 43.74,
          "en": "And then here you only have the pointers in your markup if you have really simple logic like maybe here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 43.74,
          "end": 50.37,
          "en": "where we really just update created contacts, then I would still recommend using such a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 50.37,
          "end": 53.64,
          "en": "But you can also use an inline function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 53.64,
          "end": 59.01,
          "en": "For this, you can use the modern JavaScript arrow function syntax which looks like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 59.8,
          "end": 63.82,
          "en": "And now here I'm getting some autocompletion, which I don't want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 63.85,
          "end": 67.06,
          "en": "We can avoid this by wrapping this in quotes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 68.5,
          "end": 76,
          "en": "This arrow function works such that here is the list of arguments so we could accept event here because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 76,
          "end": 76.93,
          "en": "we are getting this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 76.93,
          "end": 79.27,
          "en": "I don't need it here, but we're still getting this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 79.27,
          "end": 85.75,
          "en": "And then here you have your function code and for short statements you can now just put your syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 85.75,
          "end": 86.08,
          "en": "in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 86.08,
          "end": 88.33,
          "en": "You can even write multi-line statements here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 88.33,
          "end": 94.33,
          "en": "But the more logic you put in here, the more I would recommend that you instead just point at a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 94.33,
          "end": 95.86,
          "en": "and have your logic up there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 95.86,
          "end": 102.43,
          "en": "But if it's really short, kind of a rule of thumb, if it fits into one line, then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 102.93,
          "end": 105,
          "en": "You can just do it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 107.95,
          "end": 111.52000000000001,
          "en": "And for example, use the logic from up there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 111.97,
          "end": 114.28,
          "en": "Let me copy that for delete first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 115.24000000000001,
          "end": 116.41,
          "en": "And put it in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 116.83,
          "end": 122.05,
          "en": "Now, if you do that and you save this and I add my cards.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 126.05,
          "end": 129.17,
          "en": "And I have an error here on prevent default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 141.01,
          "end": 142.36,
          "en": "Now add my card.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 142.39,
          "end": 148.99,
          "en": "If I delete first, this still works as before, but now I'm doing this inline with this arrow function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 149.44,
          "end": 155.41,
          "en": "Now if it's only one statement as it is here, you can even omit these curly braces here because then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 155.41,
          "end": 160.12,
          "en": "this is treated as a statement, as the only statement of this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 160.12,
          "end": 162.04,
          "en": "The result of this will be returned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 162.07,
          "end": 163.51,
          "en": "Here we have no result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 163.51,
          "end": 164.37,
          "en": "Doesn't matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 164.38,
          "end": 166.3,
          "en": "So now this will still work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 166.3,
          "end": 171.28,
          "en": "And this is an alternative for very short and concise statements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 171.28,
          "end": 176.2,
          "en": "You can write them as inline functions here right on your click listener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 176.2,
          "end": 181.69,
          "en": "Again, my recommendation for most functions would be that you instead point at a function which is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 181.69,
          "end": 182.72,
          "en": "defined up there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 182.74,
          "end": 185.56,
          "en": "I find this to be clearer and easier to read.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 185.59,
          "end": 188.74,
          "en": "Nonetheless, it is worth knowing this syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
